+{"id":"BT-68","type":null,"status":"pending","priority":"P2","title":"P2 — boardctl update --note REPLACES foreman_note (silent loss) and a concurrent writer clobbers it; accepted flags are missing from help","detail":{"fingerprint":"3bf2965f6a4bb5ec0bb2d2edb712092b22c8b5f4214e7b08d728f73bbdb83734"},"created_at":"2026-09-26T22:52:34Z","created_by":null,"reasoning":"Observed live 2026-09-26 while recording SCHED-GAP-1614 on the scheduler board. Three distinct behaviours, all reproducible by reading the row back after each write:\n1. 'boardctl update <id> --note <text>' REPLACES the row's foreman_note instead of appending. A 2616-char note was replaced by a 1633-char addendum; the earlier text was only recoverable from git history. For a field that foremen use to accumulate evidence, replace-semantics silently destroys prior findings.\n2. A lane writing the same board row between two of my writes clobbered the note I had just verified (2616 + 1633 chars in, 277 chars on disk out). Last-writer-wins on a whole row means two writers lose each other's evidence with no error.\n3. 'boardctl create' ACCEPTS --priority, --status and --reasoning (proven: a scratch board row created with --priority P1 came back P1, while the default is P2, and --reasoning text persisted) but 'boardctl help create' does not list them — which is how BT-060's 'create cannot express priority' conclusion was reached incorrectly. 'create' also writes a 'repo' key that is outside the board canon, producing a standing validator warning on every row it files.\nAsk: (a) make --note append with an explicit separator (or refuse when a note exists unless --replace is passed); (b) document every accepted flag in help, and validate/warn on title-vs-field disagreement (the D6 title/priority contradictions); (c) drop the 'repo' key or declare it in the canon.","complexity":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-26T22:52:34Z","worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null,"foreman_note":null,"completed_at":null,"worktree":null,"branch":null,"sessions":null}
